I don't have your current `PlantsList.jsx` file — it hasn't been shared in this conversation. Could you paste it so I can make the exact edit you're describing? I want to make sure I preserve your existing status-clear logic, `confirmingId` handling, focus behavior, and `aria-live` setup rather than guessing at the implementation.

In the meantime, the core idea is straightforward. You'd add a counter ref and append it to the status text (or use it as a `key` on the status element) so the browser treats repeated identical messages as new content:

```jsx
const announceCount = useRef(0);

// wherever you set the status message:
announceCount.current += 1;
setStatus(`Plant added successfully (${announceCount.current})`);
```

Or, if you don't want visible counter text, use the counter as a `key` to force React to remount the `<p>`, which re-triggers the `aria-live` announcement:

```jsx
<p role="status" aria-live="polite" key={announceCount.current}>
  {status}
</p>
```

Either approach works. Paste your file and I'll wire it into your actual code.
